{{!
    @template local_moodesk/kb_language_badge

    Knowledge base — the language badge on a card, a result or a pill (KB-06).

    Rendered only for a row whose language is not the reader's: the code is
    what is seen (`PT-BR`), the language's own name is what is read aloud and
    shown on hover, and the `lang` attribute lets a screen reader say the
    name in that language.

    Context variables:
      * code     - The code, upper-cased, `_` as `-` (EN, PT-BR)
      * name     - The language's localised name (Português - Brasil)
      * htmllang - The HTML lang attribute value (pt)

    Example context (json):
    { "code": "PT-BR", "name": "Português - Brasil", "htmllang": "pt" }
}}
<span class="mhd-pill mhd-pill--outline mhd-kb-lang-badge" title="{{name}}"><span aria-hidden="true">{{code}}</span><span class="mhd-sr-only" lang="{{htmllang}}">{{name}}</span></span>
